ames_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "31000"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "31104"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "31194"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258609"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "306066"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "354150"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19001710"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/157"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Beach Volleyball, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 July – 10 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2172"} "Eiffel Tower Stadium (Champ de Mars), Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2002200"} "48 from 18 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Top 16 teams from round-robin pools advanced to the single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Twenty four teams, consisting of 48 athletes from 18 NOCs, competed in the event. The top five ranked teams were as follows: #1 – Sweden with " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504044"} "David Åhman"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504045"} "Jonatan Hellvig"] ", the 2023 world silver medalists and the #1 team in the world ranking since April 2024; #2 – Norway with " [:a {:href "/athletes/2103996"} "Anders Mol"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/145687"} "Christian Sørum"] ", the defending gold medalists and the 2022 World champions; #3 – Germany with " [:a {:href "/athletes/155263"} "Nils Ehlers"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/143391"} "Clemens Wickler"] ", who would win the 2024 European Championship, just after the Olympics; #4 – Brazil with " [:a {:href "/athletes/2103064"} "George Wanderley"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/155199"} "André Stein"] ", the 2022 World bronze medalists; and #5 – Czechia with " [:a {:href "/athletes/142091"} "Ondřej Perušič"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/142090"} "David Schweiner"] ", the 2023 World Champions. All these five top-ranked teams, plus the French team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/2103408"} "Arnaud Gauthier-Rat"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/155252"} "Youssef Krou"] ", were top seeded in the draw of the six pools."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the preliminary round, there was one big surprise to report, as the top seeded Swedish and Brazilian teams qualified for the Round of 16 only as the two best-ranked third-placed teams, after losing 2 of their 3 matches. On their home soil, the two French teams were eliminated without being able to win a single match, while " [:a {:href "/athletes/155378"} "Miles Evans"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/155375"} "Chase Budinger"] " (USA) and cousins " [:a {:href "/athletes/133114"} "Esteban Grimalt"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/133115"} "Marco Grimalt"] " (CHI) won the lucky loser round and qualified for the Round of 16."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the knockout stage, the world #1 team, the Swedes, lost only one set against the Cubans " [:a {:href "/athletes/155217"} "Noslen Díaz"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2502832"} "Jorge Alayo"] " in the round of 16. Then, they successively beat the Brazilians in the quarter-finals, the Qataris, " [:a {:href "/athletes/135614"} "Cherif Younousse"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/146090"} "Ahmed Tijan"] ", in the semi-finals, and the Germans in the final to claim Olympic gold."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Norway, the reigning Olympic champions and 2022 World Champions, took the bronze medal by defeating Qatar. There were no big surprises, as the top three teams in the world ranking made the podium."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button485914", :class "btn btn-default"} "Detai